# agentlabs.cc serves its own demo videos from public/agentpod/*.mp4 (verified
# live, see .github/workflows/deploy.yml deploy-agentlabs). Without a
# .vercelignore of its own, Vercel falls back to the repo-root .vercelignore
# ("If there is no .vercelignore to be found at the project level, Vercel
# will use the .vercelignore at the root level" —
# https://vercel.com/docs/deployments/vercel-ignore). That root file excludes
# `public/*.mp4` / `public/*.webm` for vibebrowser.app, which serves no local
# video and redirects to dl.agentlabs.cc instead. Applied to this project's
# own rootDirectory (apps/agentlabs), the same glob silently stripped its
# real demo videos from every deploy — the "Media pointer guard" step then
# failed because the build output legitimately contained none. This file
# exists purely to opt agentlabs OUT of inheriting that rule; keep it empty
# (or add agentlabs-specific ignores here, never the video globs).
